# Cloudflare's Email Address Obfuscation (Scrape Shield) rewrites every email in the served
# HTML into <a href="/cdn-cgi/l/email-protection#<hash>">. On Cloudflare **Pages** that endpoint
# is not served, so every such link returns 404 — 6 of them live, on 4 pages including the
# homepage. Bingbot hit exactly those on 2026-09-25 (CrawledPages=4, Code4xx=2).
# Real browsers never navigate here (email-decode.min.js reads the hash off the DOM and swaps
# in the mailto:), so this rule only affects crawlers and no-JS visitors: 404 -> 301 instead.
/cdn-cgi/l/email-protection   /about  301
/cdn-cgi/l/email-protection/* /about  301
